<title>MEXICO: Mexico places all $200 mln in dollar put options.</title>
<headline>Mexico places all $200 mln in dollar put options.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's central bank said Monday it placed all $200 million in dollar put options that it offered in its September auction.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, Banco de Mexico said the options, a scheme devised by the central bank to build up foreign reserves, were placed at a weighted premium of 10.18 pesos per $1,000.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530</p>
